# API Layer Patterns

## Architecture Overview

The API layer has 5 files that work together:

```
src/api/
  config.js      — env vars, base URL, auth headers
  client.js      — ApiClient class for real StackRox Central API
  mockClient.js  — MockApiClient reading from src/mockData.js
  liveSync.js    — polls real API + merges into shared mock arrays
  index.js       — UnifiedApiClient that delegates to real or mock
  hooks.js       — React hooks wrapping the unified client
  reportStore.js — in-memory report configuration store
```

## Mock + Live Merge Strategy

The core pattern: live data from StackRox replaces mock data, BUT mock-only rows are preserved.

### MOCK_ID_PREFIX

```js
const MOCK_ID_PREFIX = /^(cluster-|ns-|deploy-|v-|pol-|exc-|filter-|report-|col-)/;
```

Any row whose `id` matches this regex is prototype-only mock data. During merge, these rows are kept even when live data arrives. This lets valuable mock entries (like sample saved filters, demo reports) coexist with real API data.

### mergeArrayById

```js
function mergeArrayById(target, liveItems, idKey = "id") {
  const liveIds = new Set(liveItems.map((item) => item[idKey]));
  const mockOnly = target.filter(
    (item) => !liveIds.has(item[idKey]) && MOCK_ID_PREFIX.test(item[idKey] || "")
  );
  target.length = 0;
  target.push(...liveItems, ...mockOnly);
}
```

This mutates the shared array in-place so all consumers see the update without re-importing.

## Never Remove Mocks

When connecting to a real StackRox Central, NEVER remove mock data from `src/mockData.js`. The prototype needs both:
- Real data for fidelity comparison
- Mock data for demo scenarios (saved filters, sample reports, edge-case CVEs)

The `UnifiedApiClient` in `index.js` handles this by merging live results with mock-only rows for alerts, policies, and exceptions. Saved filters and generated reports stay mock-only.

## syncState.version for Re-renders

`liveSync.js` increments `syncVersion` after each successful sync. Components must include this in their `useMemo` dependencies:

```jsx
const syncState = useLiveSync();

const data = useMemo(() => {
  return someComputation(rawData);
}, [rawData, syncState.version]);  // version triggers re-compute after sync
```

Without `syncState.version`, the UI won't update when `liveSync` mutates the shared arrays in-place.

## Adding a New Data Type

1. Add mock data to `src/mockData.js` with IDs matching `MOCK_ID_PREFIX`
2. Add real API method to `src/api/client.js`
3. Add mock API method to `src/api/mockClient.js`
4. Add sync call to `doSync()` in `src/api/liveSync.js` using `mergeArrayById`
5. Add unified method to `UnifiedApiClient` in `src/api/index.js` with merge/fallback
6. Add hook to `src/api/hooks.js`

## Proxy Configuration

When `VITE_STACKROX_URL` is set, `vite.config.js` proxies `/stackrox-api` to that URL. The `ApiClient` in `client.js` uses `/stackrox-api` as its base path. Auth is via Bearer token from `VITE_STACKROX_TOKEN`.

## Polling

`liveSync.js` polls on `API_CONFIG.pollInterval` (default 30s, configurable via `VITE_SYNC_INTERVAL`). Each poll runs `Promise.allSettled` for all data types so one failure doesn't block others.

## Status Flow

```
idle → syncing → connected (success) or error (failure)
         ↑                    |
         └────────────────────┘  (next poll interval)
```

When not configured: status stays `"mock"` permanently.
